WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.690
An invoice tells a customer what they owe, and gives them a link to pay it.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.353
A receipt proves that a payment arrived.

00:00:08.353 --> 00:00:12.580
This video shows how to brand them, send an invoice, how a customer

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:17.270
pays from the link, and how receipts and refund notices reach the customer.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:27.750
Customers who pay later need to know exactly what they owe, to whom, and by when.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.950
They want to pay without hunting for a password, even from a forwarded email.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.760
And when a payment arrives, they want proof, with a number they can quote.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.444
Invoices and receipts give you all of that, with your business's name and

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.130
details on every one.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:55.413
An invoice gets its number, such as INV-1001, the first time the customer

00:00:55.413 --> 00:00:58.630
is told about a payment they pay themselves.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:05.790
Every reminder and invoice carries a pay link that works without signing in, for sixty days.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:13.451
A receipt, such as R-1001, is sent after every payment, however it was paid.

00:01:13.451 --> 00:01:16.570
A refund sends a refund notice.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.830
All of them print cleanly, with one set of branding settings.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.263
Invoices and receipts share one set of branding settings.

00:01:30.263 --> 00:01:32.919
Open Settings, Commerce, Receipts.

00:01:32.919 --> 00:01:37.965
The Business name, Business address and Logo URL are shown at the top.

00:01:37.965 --> 00:01:43.410
The contact email, phone, website and footer text are printed at the bottom.

00:01:43.862 --> 00:01:49.537
Header title is the heading of every receipt, Payment receipt unless you change it.

00:01:49.537 --> 00:01:51.706
Invoices always say Invoice.

00:01:51.706 --> 00:01:57.318
The test-payment badge marks receipts for payments made in a provider's test mode.

00:01:57.318 --> 00:01:58.402
Click Save.

00:02:02.575 --> 00:02:07.623
Open Commerce, Transactions, and a payment the customer pays themselves, such as a

00:02:07.623 --> 00:02:10.033
bank transfer waiting for its money.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:14.278
On its page, Send invoice sends the customer the invoice now, with a

00:02:14.278 --> 00:02:15.655
link that pays it.

00:02:16.488 --> 00:02:20.412
The transaction now has an invoice number, shown as Invoice.

00:02:20.412 --> 00:02:21.245
Open it.

00:02:21.245 --> 00:02:26.181
The invoice carries your logo, name and address, the invoice number and date,

00:02:26.181 --> 00:02:30.165
who it is billed to, its status, the lines, the total and the

00:02:30.165 --> 00:02:32.068
due date, and your footer.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.881
Print invoice prints only the invoice, without the site's menus.

00:02:36.881 --> 00:02:41.864
Under Payment link, Copy puts the customer's pay link on the clipboard, to

00:02:41.864 --> 00:02:43.421
paste into a reply.

00:02:43.421 --> 00:02:45.290
It works for sixty days.

00:02:49.481 --> 00:02:52.971
The customer opens the link, with no account or password.

00:02:52.971 --> 00:02:56.793
The page shows what the payment is for, the Amount due, the Due

00:02:56.793 --> 00:03:00.061
on date, and a Pay button, with the invoice under it.

00:03:00.515 --> 00:03:03.241
Pay opens checkout with the balance ready.

00:03:03.241 --> 00:03:07.785
A customer who decides not to pay now has a Back to the payment page link.

00:03:11.988 --> 00:03:17.299
When the money arrives, open the transaction, enter the amount and a reference

00:03:17.299 --> 00:03:22.168
under Record an offline payment, and click Record payment, and confirm.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:28.510
With Send Payment Receipts on, the customer is sent a receipt after every payment:

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:32.057
online, charged to a card, or recorded by hand.

00:03:32.057 --> 00:03:35.671
Each receipt has its own number, such as R-1001.

00:03:35.671 --> 00:03:41.560
In the transaction's timeline, the payment links to its receipt with View receipt.

00:03:42.011 --> 00:03:43.717
View receipt opens it:

00:03:43.717 --> 00:03:48.226
your branding, the receipt number and date, who it is billed to, the

00:03:48.226 --> 00:03:51.273
amount paid, and notes such as Paid offline.

00:03:51.273 --> 00:03:53.101
Print receipt prints it.

00:03:57.301 --> 00:04:01.275
When a refund of a payment succeeds, the customer is told, with the

00:04:01.275 --> 00:04:05.631
amount, and that it can take a few business days to reach their statement.

00:04:06.381 --> 00:04:10.247
A receipt for a payment made in a provider's test mode carries a

00:04:10.247 --> 00:04:13.341
Test payment badge, unless you turn the badge off.

00:04:14.091 --> 00:04:17.002
Pay links use your site's public address.

00:04:17.002 --> 00:04:21.461
Set the Base url under Settings, General, before you rely on them.

00:04:25.661 --> 00:04:27.187
A service business:

00:04:27.187 --> 00:04:32.071
send an invoice with a pay link, and the customer pays without signing in.

00:04:32.821 --> 00:04:35.010
A company that pays slowly:

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:39.521
reminders carry the same link, so the newest one always works.

00:04:40.271 --> 00:04:41.351
A bookkeeper:

00:04:41.351 --> 00:04:44.251
every payment has a numbered receipt to file.

00:04:45.001 --> 00:04:45.778
A shop:

00:04:45.778 --> 00:04:50.141
customers print their own invoices and receipts from their account.

00:04:52.141 --> 00:04:57.104
With invoices and receipts, you ask for payment clearly, and prove it arrived.

00:04:57.104 --> 00:04:58.641
Thanks for watching.

